  "prompt_text": "Use case: style-transfer. Transform the supplied deer sheet into another complete game animal sprite sheet, retaining the exact 2 rows by 5 columns, consistent scale, fine controlled sepia ink and restrained two-tone earth-colour washes. First image is layout/animal-style reference; person and scene are locked STYLE ONLY, never include their background. Actual transparent RGBA, no text, no labels, no grid, no ground, no shadow, no halo. Exactly TEN isolated whole figures with generous transparent gutters and margins, fully connected hooves/tail/horns. Top row SOUTH: front three-quarter 35degrees toward viewer LEFT from head-on, both chest and side visible. Lower row EAST: side three-quarter facing RIGHT. Same slightly elevated ~20degree camera, light upper left. Main contour twice interior line. Short hide: exactly3 small clusters of2-3 marks on shoulder/flank/haunch, diagonal upper-left to lower-right. Broad quiet washes, no all-over fur, not 3D or photorealism. Columns BOTH ROWS: 1 STAND,4 grounded hooves, alert; 2 WALK, obvious raised bent forehoof and opposite hind step; 3 RUN, airborne extended gallop, forelegs forward hindlegs back; 4 GRAZE, muzzle lowered completely to hoof level with bent neck, no grass; 5 DEAD, horizontal limp on side, legs sideways, eyes closed, no blood. Identical body size/proportions across upright poses. Designed to reduce to96x80frames; strong readable anatomy. SUBJECT: primitive domestic DONKEY, warm slate-grey body, pale parchment muzzle/eye rims/underside, long upright ears with dark tips, short coarse dark mane, narrow dark dorsal stripe and small shoulder cross, thin tail ending in black tuft. Donkey proportions: slightly small heavy head, compact sturdy body, fine legs, small single equine hooves. Always two very long donkey ears, no horns. Natural early domesticate, no tack, bridle, bells, shoes, harness or saddle. Mane only3 groups of3 marks.\n",
